  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Voxtalisib may interact with the Sodium- and chloride-dependent GABA transporter 1 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is predicted to target the Sodium channel subunit beta-2, which in turn is a target of a compound (Npc11947) that itself targets the GABA transporter. Similarly, Voxtalisib is also predicted to interact with another Sodium channel protein, which is a target of trans-2-hydroxycinnamic acid, which also targets the GABA transporter. These findings indicate that Voxtalisib may influence the function of the GABA transporter through different sodium channel-related mechanisms. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role for Voxtalisib in modulating the activity of the GABA transporter via sodium channel interactions. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are similar across different paths, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain due to the complexity of the signaling pathways involved.",
